CORE unix
main.c
--unwind 8 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ assertion .*: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\[main\.assertion\.[1-4]\] .*: FAILURE$
--
strtol_l converts as strtol does; the locale argument is not read.
strtol_l and locale_t are POSIX (<stdlib.h>, <locale.h>); Windows has
_strtol_l with _locale_t instead, hence the unix tag.
